---
description: Never show raw IDs/UUIDs in UI — always use readable labels
globs: app/**/*.{tsx,ts}
alwaysApply: true
---

# No raw IDs in UI

Users must never see opaque identifiers (UUIDs, `sp-…`, `scamp-…`, URN fragments, etc.) as the primary label in selects, tables, badges, titles, or empty states. Show human-readable details instead.

## Do

- Resolve entities to a label helper before render (`socialEventCardLabel`, `socialAccountLabel`, `socialPostLabel`, resource title, person name…).
- For Base UI / shadcn `Select`, pass readable children to `SelectValue` (the trigger does **not** auto-map `SelectItem` children from the raw `value`).
- When the entity is missing, use i18n fallbacks (`unknown_card`, `no_card`, “Untitled…”) — never the id string.
- Keep ids only in `value` / `key` / IPC payloads / `data-*` attributes for logic.

## Don’t

```tsx
// Bad — trigger shows the UUID
<Select value={cardId}>
  <SelectTrigger><SelectValue /></SelectTrigger>
  <SelectContent>
    {cards.map((c) => (
      <SelectItem key={c.id} value={c.id}>{c.internalName}</SelectItem>
    ))}
  </SelectContent>
</Select>

// Bad — fallback paints the id into the UI
socialEventCardLabel(card ?? { internalName: cardId, title: '', slug: null })
```

```tsx
// Good
const selected = cards.find((c) => c.id === cardId);
<Select value={cardId}>
  <SelectTrigger>
    <SelectValue>{selected ? socialEventCardLabel(selected) : t('social.events.unknown_card')}</SelectValue>
  </SelectTrigger>
  …
</Select>
```

If a label helper might receive an id as a name field, reject opaque ids (`looksLikeOpaqueId`) and fall back to a placeholder.
